WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.077
Organizational Profiles turn CSF 2.0 from a reference framework into an operating tool.

2
00:00:06.077 --> 00:00:13.890
A Current Profile describes the cybersecurity outcomes an organization is currently achieving, partially achieving, or attempting to achieve.

3
00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:16.494
It should be honest and evidence-based.

4
00:00:16.494 --> 00:00:20.835
The purpose is not to make the organization look mature.

5
00:00:20.835 --> 00:00:25.609
The purpose is to understand current risk and support better decisions.

6
00:00:25.609 --> 00:00:28.648
A Target Profile describes desired cybersecurity outcomes.

7
00:00:28.648 --> 00:00:36.461
Those desired outcomes should reflect business objectives, risk tolerance, requirements, threat context, technology, supplier dependencies, and available resources.

8
00:00:36.461 --> 00:00:41.669
A Target Profile is not necessarily every possible outcome at maximum rigor.

9
00:00:41.669 --> 00:00:48.614
It is the set of outcomes the organization decides it needs for the scope being assessed.

10
00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:53.823
Comparing a Current Profile to a Target Profile reveals gaps and priorities.

11
00:00:53.823 --> 00:00:59.466
Some gaps may be urgent because they affect critical assets or high-risk suppliers.

12
00:00:59.466 --> 00:01:08.147
Others may be acceptable for a period of time if an owner documents the risk decision and the improvement plan.

13
00:01:08.147 --> 00:01:18.564
This comparison helps teams move from general concern to specific work: what outcome is missing, who owns it, what evidence exists, what improvement is

14
00:01:18.564 --> 00:01:21.603
planned, and when progress will be reviewed.

15
00:01:21.603 --> 00:01:24.641
Profiles can be scoped in many ways.

16
00:01:24.641 --> 00:01:35.058
A profile might cover an entire organization, a business unit, a product, a cloud environment, a critical system, a supplier relationship, or a threat

17
00:01:35.058 --> 00:01:35.492
scenario.

18
00:01:35.492 --> 00:01:40.267
The scope should be documented clearly, along with assumptions and exclusions.

19
00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:47.646
A well-scoped Organizational Profile helps leaders, engineers, and risk teams communicate about the same set of outcomes.
